{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the existing built-in prior sampling statements for `a`, `b`, and `sigma` so that each parameter is given its prior before being used to compute `y_pred` or in the protected-data likelihood. This preserves the same posterior/log density because the sampling statements are the same and only their order changed. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> a;
  real<lower=0> b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  vector[N] y_pred;
  a ~ normal(0, 10);
  b ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y_pred = a * exp(-b * x);
  y ~ lognormal(log(y_pred), sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":6,"x":[4.552316017791849,2.6843484495313894,6.6523665321817145,4.874270756968872,6.289040368147003,2.3200669581081237],"y":[6.0,5.0,6.0,5.0,6.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
